<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela bolivar softens to 469.75/471.00/dlr.</title>
<headline>Venezuela bolivar softens to 469.75/471.00/dlr.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan bolivar softened gently to a Central Bank-set ceiling of 469.75/471.00 bolivars per dollar on seasonal corporate dollar demand, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Demand grew steadily throughout the afternoon, which is when the Central Bank started supplying dollars,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>&quot;But the session was nothing unusual -- it followed a normal pattern of demand for the Venezuelan economy,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>On Friday the bolivar closed at 469.50/470.75 per dollar.</p>
<p>-- Silene Ramirez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
